<misterromdescription>
    <name>Raiden Fighters 2 (Europe, SPI cartridge, pre-flashed)</name>
    <setname>rdft2</setname>
    <rbf>SeibuSPI</rbf>
    <mameversion>0277</mameversion>
    <year>1997</year>
    <manufacturer>Seibu Kaihatsu</manufacturer>
    <players>2</players>
    <joystick>8</joystick>
    <rotation>vertical (cw)</rotation>
    <region>Europe</region>
    <category>Shooter</category>

    <!--
      INCOMPLETE. This MRA loads rdft2 correctly, and that is all it does so
      far. The core still fetches sprites at the SEI252 4 MB chunk stride and
      decrypts tiles and sprites with the SEI252 keys, so rdft2's graphics will
      be wrong on screen until spi_sprite takes SPR_CHUNK_STRIDE as a port and
      the RISE10 unit and rdft2 tile keys are selected. See PLAN.md "what rdft2
      still needs". Everything below is verified; nothing below is the reason
      it does not run yet.
    -->

    <!--
      LIKE rdft, THE CARTRIDGE HAS NO SAMPLE ROM: the YMF271 plays out of two
      Intel E28F008SA flash chips the game programs itself on first boot. This
      MRA ships that flash pre-programmed so the several-minute reflash is
      skipped.

      UNLIKE rdft, the image is not a concatenation. Only the first 1.5 MB is a
      copy; the remaining half megabyte is DECOMPRESSED from sound1.u0222 by a
      routine in the game's own 386 program. An MRA cannot express that, so the
      core does it during the download -- rtl/spi_rom_decode.sv, selected by
      the codec config below. The format is byte pair encoding over DPCM, read
      off the 386 at 0x2A1D20; PLAN.md section 0 has the derivation.

        flash[0x000000-0x000003] = maincpu[0x1FFFFC-0x1FFFFF]   region + build
        flash[0x000004-0x17C246] = pcm.u0217[4..]               verbatim
        flash[0x17C247-0x1EF333] = decode(sound1.u0222[0..0x4C664])
        flash[0x1EF334-0x1FFFFF] = 0xFF, erased and never addressed

      The whole 2 MB is reproduced bit-for-bit offline by
      tools/build_soundflash.py, checked by sha256 against the image MAME's own
      flash devices end up holding, and the core's decoder is checked against
      the same reference (`make -C sim run-bpe`).

      The four header bytes are the region lock, not a checksum: a verbatim
      copy of the last four bytes of the 386 program, region byte plus build
      ID. A stamp that does not match the program makes the game reflash, so
      this image belongs to THIS set's program ROMs and no other region's.

      The erased tail is not padded here. Nothing addresses it -- it is past
      the end of the samples -- and writing 68 KB of 0xFF would mean hardcoding
      the decoder's OUTPUT length into rom_loader's table, where every other
      number is an input length. If it is ever wanted, the clean way is a fill
      scatter mode that consumes no download bytes at all.
    -->

    <!--
      Part order is significant. rtl/rom_loader.sv walks this list with a fixed
      table -- selected by the mod byte below -- and performs MAME's
      ROM_LOAD24_* / ROM_LOAD32_* byte scatter in hardware, because MRA
      <interleave> cannot express the 3-byte period the Seibu "D + P" graphics
      ROM pairs need. Do not reorder or insert parts without updating the
      rdft2 table in rom_loader.sv to match. `make check-mra` checks them
      against each other and against MAME's driver.

      Layout produced in SDRAM (see rtl/spi_defs.vh):
        0x0000000  2 MB   386 program
        0x0200000  256 KB Z80 program -- RAM, NOT loaded here. The 386 fills it
                          through port 0x688 and releases the Z80 with 0x68C.
        0x0240000  192 KB text tiles
        0x0280000  2 MB   YMF271 samples: the pre-programmed flash image
        0x0500000  12 MB  background tiles, two 6 MB groups
        0x1100000  18 MB  sprites, three 6 MB plane-pair chunks
    -->

    <!--
      Mod byte 0x03: bit 0 selects the SXX2C cartridge board wiring, bits 3:1
      select set 1 on that board, which is rdft2. rdft.mra sends 0x01 (same
      board, set 0) and rdfts.mra sends nothing at all.

      The second element is the codec config: pairs of {part index, codec id}.
      Part 13 is the compressed sample tail, and codec 1 is CODEC_BPE_DPCM.
      Parts default to codec 0, a straight copy, so nothing else is listed.
      Ids live in rtl/spi_defs.vh and the decoders in rtl/spi_rom_decode.sv.

      IT MUST COME BEFORE THE index="0" ROM. Main_MiSTer sends the <rom>
      elements in file order, so an index-1 that follows the image arrives
      AFTER the loader has already walked its table -- the download then runs
      against the wrong layout and every part after the first lands wrong.
    -->
    <rom index="1">
        <part>03</part>
        <part>0D 01</part>
    </rom>

    <rom index="0" zip="rdft2.zip" md5="none">
        <!-- 386 program: four byte lanes -->
        <part name="prg0.tun" crc="3cb3fdca"/>
        <part name="prg1.bin" crc="cab55d88"/>
        <part name="prg2.bin" crc="83758b0e"/>
        <part name="prg3.bin" crc="084fb5e4"/>

        <!-- text layer: three byte lanes, and the lane order is 1, 0, 2 -->
        <part name="fix0.u0524" crc="6fdf4cf6"/>
        <part name="fix1.u0518" crc="69b7899b"/>
        <part name="fixp.u0514" crc="99a5fece"/>

        <!-- background tiles: 12 MB, two D+P groups 6 MB apart -->
        <part name="bg-1d.u0535" crc="6143f576"/>
        <part name="bg-1p.u0537" crc="55e64ef7"/>
        <part name="bg-2d.u0536" crc="c607a444"/>
        <part name="bg-2p.u0538" crc="f0830248"/>

        <!--
          Sprites: 18 MB in three 6 MB plane-pair chunks, and MAME's order is
          obj3, obj2, obj1 -- chunk 0 is obj3, not obj1. The chunks are
          contiguous at this stride, so the loader places all six as one run.
        -->
        <part name="obj3.u0434"  crc="e08f42dc"/>
        <part name="obj3b.u0433" crc="1b6a523c"/>
        <part name="obj2.u0431"  crc="7aeadd8e"/>
        <part name="obj2b.u0432" crc="5d790a5d"/>
        <part name="obj1.u0429"  crc="c2c50f02"/>
        <part name="obj1b.u0430" crc="5259321f"/>

        <!--
          YMF271 sample flash, pre-programmed. Loader part 12: the region stamp
          plus 0x17C243 bytes of pcm.u0217 at identity offset, 4 + 0x17C243 =
          0x17C247.
        -->
        <part>80 4A 4A 37</part>
        <part name="pcm.u0217" crc="2edc30b5" offset="0x000004" length="0x17C243"/>

        <!--
          Loader part 13, CODEC_BPE_DPCM: the compressed tail. 0x4C665 bytes in,
          0x730ED out. This is a LENGTH-LIMITED slice on purpose -- the rest of
          sound1.u0222 is not sample data. 0x60000-0x7FFFF is rdft2's Z80
          program, which the 386 downloads over port 0x688 at runtime rather
          than the loader placing it, exactly as on rdft.
        -->
        <part name="sound1.u0222" crc="b7bd3703" length="0x04C665"/>
    </rom>

    <!--
      Same control layout as rdft; the names map to joystick bits 4 upwards IN
      ORDER and SeibuSPI.sv decodes them at exactly those positions.
    -->
    <buttons names="Shot,Bomb,Button 3,Start,Coin,Service Coin,Test"
             default="A,B,X,Start,Select,R,L" count="3"/>

    <switches default="00" base="0">
        <dip name="Flip Screen"  bits="0" ids="Off,On"/>
        <dip name="Service Mode" bits="1" ids="Off,On"/>
    </switches>
</misterromdescription>
